From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:48:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: use the battery's constant charge
 current

The init sequence caps the fast charge current at 1 A, whatever the
battery is rated for. power_supply_get_battery_info() already gives the
driver the battery's constant-charge-current-max-microamp, so program
that when the battery specifies it, up to the 4.5 A the downstream
driver allows. Batteries without the property keep the 1 A cap.

The comma four's firmware and downstream kernel run the charger at 2 A,
and its device tree can now say so.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index f58c51ad92..be45d9545f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 
 #define FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_CFG				0x61
 #define FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_SETTING_MASK		GENMASK(7, 0)
+#define FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_MAX_UA			4500000
 
 #define FLOAT_VOLTAGE_CFG				0x70
 #define FLOAT_VOLTAGE_SETTING_MASK			GENMASK(7, 0)
@@ -892,7 +893,8 @@ static const struct smb_init_register smb_init_seq[] = {
 	/*
 	 * This overrides all of the current limit options exposed to userspace
 	 * and prevents the device from pulling more than ~1A. This is done
-	 * to minimise potential fire hazard risks.
+	 * to minimise potential fire hazard risks. A battery that specifies
+	 * its constant charge current gets that instead.
 	 */
 	{ .addr = FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_CFG,
 	  .mask = FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_SETTING_MASK,
@@ -1016,6 +1018,17 @@ static int smb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (rc < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc, "Couldn't set vbat max\n");
 
+	if (chip->batt_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua > 0) {
+		rc = min(chip->batt_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua,
+			 FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_MAX_UA) / CURRENT_SCALE_FACTOR;
+		rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
+					chip->base + FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_CFG,
+					FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_SETTING_MASK, rc);
+		if (rc < 0)
+			return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
+					     "Couldn't set fast charge current\n");
+	}
+
 	rc = smb_init_irq(chip, &irq, "bat-ov", smb_handle_batt_overvoltage);
 	if (rc < 0)
 		return rc;
